+# NG-9 Narrowed: Filtering the Veterinarian Directory by Specialty Is In Scope
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declared searching for a veterinarian out of scope, alongside searching for a pet or a visit, on the ground that only owner search needed to be demonstrated. A request has since arrived to filter the veterinarian directory by specialty. This narrows NG-9 rather than reversing it: filtering the directory by an attribute it already displays is a different capability from free-text search over veterinarians.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Leave NG-9 whole and decline the request** — keeps the non-goal table unchanged, but refuses a capability the product owner has asked for.
+2. **Reverse NG-9 entirely** — makes veterinarians searchable, which overshoots the request and pulls in free-text search that no one asked for.
+3. **Narrow NG-9** — free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope; filtering the directory by a specialty it already shows comes in. This matches the request exactly.
+
+## Decision
+
+We narrow NG-9. Free-text search over veterinarians remains out of scope. Filtering the veterinarian directory by the whole specialty name — an attribute the directory already displays — is in scope and is captured as REQ-VET-003.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The Non-Goals table's NG-9 row now excludes only free-text search over veterinarians, pets, and visits; attribute filtering of a directory the system already shows is no longer covered by it.
+- The filter is a URL contract only; no page control accompanies it in this decision. A visible control, should one be wanted, is a separate future request.
+- The distinction — search versus attribute filter — is the line NG-9 now draws, and it must hold if further directory filters are proposed.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+## References
+
+- [PRD: Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the requirement this narrowing brings into scope
+- [system-design.md § Contracts](../system-design.md#contracts) — the vet directory contracts that realize the specialty filter
