 ### Veterinarian directory
 
-<a id="req-vet-001"></a>
+<a id="req-vet-001"></a><a id="req-vet-003"></a>
 
-The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`.
+The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`. The same directory is also served as a machine-readable document at a JSON endpoint — a supported surface returning the same veterinarians `[REQ-VET-003]`.
+
+Either surface can be narrowed to one specialty. Both accept an optional specialty filter supplied on the request: the page or document then shows only the veterinarians holding that specialty, and without the filter each behaves as it does today `[REQ-VET-003]`. The filter matches the whole specialty name and ignores letter case; a value that is only part of a specialty name does not match. Leading and trailing spaces around a non-blank value are disregarded, the way they are for an owner search, so a padded specialty name matches the same veterinarians as the unpadded one. A blank or space-only value is treated as no filter, the way an empty owner search is. A specialty no veterinarian holds is not an error: the surface returns its normal, successful response with an empty list of veterinarians. On the HTML page the filter carries across the page-at-a-time links, so a filtered result stays filtered as the reader moves between pages. The filter is a request contract only; neither surface gains a form, dropdown, or other page control in this capability `[REQ-VET-003]`.
 
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given the clinic's veterinarians, when the directory is opened, then each name and its specialties are listed a page at a time.
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is shown as having none.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given no specialty filter, when the directory page is opened then it lists every veterinarian a page at a time as it does today, and when the JSON endpoint is requested then it returns every veterinarian.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty that some veterinarians hold, when the directory page is opened with that filter, then only those veterinarians are listed, a page at a time over the filtered list.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty that some veterinarians hold, when the JSON endpoint is requested with that filter, then only those veterinarians are returned.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a filter differing from a specialty name only by letter case, when either surface is requested, then it matches that specialty.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a filter that is only the start of a specialty name and not the whole name, when either surface is requested, then no veterinarian is matched by that partial value.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a filter no veterinarian's specialty matches, when either surface is requested, then the normal successful response is returned with an empty list of veterinarians.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a blank or space-only filter, when either surface is requested, then it behaves as if no filter were supplied.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a non-blank filter with leading or trailing spaces around a specialty name, when either surface is requested, then it matches the same veterinarians as the specialty name without them.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a filtered result spanning more than one page, when a page-at-a-time link on the HTML page is followed, then the link keeps the filter and the next page stays filtered.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. A veterinarian's specialties are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
-2. **Known defect.** A second route returns the same list in a machine-readable form. Nothing consumes it, and it carries no requirement — see the Superseded list.
+2. A veterinarian holding several specialties appears in a filtered result whenever the filtered specialty is among the ones they hold.
+3. A specialty filter that matches no veterinarian — including a value outside the clinic's specialty list — yields the normal successful response with an empty list of veterinarians, not an error.
 
